-- lib/image.cub — the C++ image (plan 10.1, 18.9, B19): a compositional translator over codes, one
-- clause per source form, one definition to one C++ entity, nothing inlined or specialized unless
-- the assignment says so. Loaded after lib/repr.cub (the whole back end).
--
-- Binding times (10.1): a parameter whose type is a universe is a template type parameter (the
-- image keeps the function uniform in a type as C++ keeps it); a parameter named `build` in the
-- assignment is a non-type template parameter (a constant the consumer's build fixes); a parameter
-- at usage 0 (a proof, a length only types mention) is absent; everything else is a run-time
-- parameter. What C++ cannot hold at any stage (dimensions, paths, Kan operations, universes as
-- values, reflection) is reported per definition: `exported`, or `not exportable` with the form.
--
-- The fragment emitted (10.1): structs and std::variant for data (one struct per constructor,
-- the type a struct holding the variant, recursive fields through std::shared_ptr since values
-- are shared at multiplicity ω), std::visit with an overload set for a case, cub::fix for a
-- structural recursion (the hypothesis is the recursive call), lambdas for λ, std::pair for pairs,
-- cub::welim for word elimination, fixed-width integers and doubles for the primitive types,
-- cub::bytes<n> (a std::array) with cub::load64/store64 whose bound is an [[assume]] inside the
-- helper — a law used by the specializer never reaches here as a comment (10.1): what survives
-- is the assume. The fragment has a parser back into codes, lib/reimport.cub, which is its
-- semantics and the check of the image.
--
-- Names are positional and reversible: g<n> for a checked definition (a table of (g , bytes)
-- may name some), D<d> for a data type, D<d>_c<c> for its constructors, f<k> for fields, v<i>
-- for variables by depth, P<i> for template parameters. The generality `specialized` (code.cub's
-- Generality) is the residue printer: the C of lib/emitu.cub over the specializer's first-order
-- form, which the fragment includes (B19's first milestone); `image` is the translation below.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- results: bytes, or a reason
-- (a pair: (0 , bytes) ok, (1 , why) not; a data type declared here would need checked field types)
xok b = (#0 , b)
xno w = (#1 , w)
xbind r f = if %weq (fst r) #0 then f (snd r) else r
xmap f r = if %weq (fst r) #0 then xok (f (snd r)) else r
xcat2 a b = xbind a (λ x → xmap (λ y → lapp x y) b)
xcat3 a b c = xcat2 a (xcat2 b c)
xcat4 a b c d = xcat2 a (xcat3 b c d)
xcat5 a b c d e = xcat2 a (xcat4 b c d e)
xcat6 a b c d e f = xcat2 a (xcat5 b c d e f)
xcat7 a b c d e f g = xcat2 a (xcat6 b c d e f g)
xs s = xok s
